Blend the menu bar and the title bar for the Agua value

The style rewrites the Agua appearance of the two title bars to the
modified Agua appearance. The value of the menu bar keeps the Agua
appearance. The test for the blend of the menu bar and the title bar
compares the raw values. The test therefore fails for a configuration
that names Agua. The blend stops, although the paint of the menu bar
makes the same modification. The decoration also loses the height of the
menu bar.

The test now compares the modified values. A configuration with Agua in
the three appearances blends again. Every other appearance keeps the
result of the test, because the modification changes the Agua value
alone.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 10 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/common.h b/qt6/common/common.h
index 4b642b2b..b8545972 100644
--- a/qt6/common/common.h
+++ b/qt6/common/common.h
@@ -97,7 +97,8 @@ enum {
 #define SUNKEN_BEVEL_DARK_ALPHA(X)  (X.value()/800.0) // 0.25
 #define SUNKEN_BEVEL_LIGHT_ALPHA(X) (X.value()/500.0) // 0.40
 
-#define BLEND_TITLEBAR     (opts.menubarAppearance==opts.titlebarAppearance && opts.menubarAppearance==opts.inactiveTitlebarAppearance && \
+#define BLEND_TITLEBAR     (MODIFY_AGUA(opts.menubarAppearance)==MODIFY_AGUA(opts.titlebarAppearance) && \
+                           MODIFY_AGUA(opts.menubarAppearance)==MODIFY_AGUA(opts.inactiveTitlebarAppearance) && \
                            !(opts.windowBorder&WINDOW_BORDER_BLEND_TITLEBAR) && SHADE_WINDOW_BORDER==opts.shadeMenubars && opts.windowDrag)
 
 #define PBAR_BORDER        4
